# The repository is edited on Windows and deployed to Linux containers.
#
# A CRLF line ending in an executable script is not cosmetic: the kernel reads
# the shebang literally, so `#!/bin/sh\r` becomes a request for an interpreter
# named "sh\r" and the container dies with a bare "no such file or directory".
# Same for the Caddyfile, whose parser treats a stray \r as part of a token.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh        text eol=lf
Caddyfile   text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.mjs       text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
